STATUS: Historical brief for the retired campaign chapter-thumbnail selector.
CampaignScreen now navigates between full-screen chapter maps; do not generate
or restore these thumbnail frames for its UI.

Generate two matching transparent overlay frames for the wide
campaign chapter-map thumbnails. One frame marks the currently selected
chapter; the other is used by every non-current chapter.

## Reference images

- Attach the user-provided campaign-screen screenshot. Use only its upper-right
  chapter selector to match the frame silhouette and selected/unselected
  treatments. Do not recreate the screen.
- Attach
  `assets_src/campaign/chapter-thumbnails/campaign_chapter_thumbnails_sheet.png`
  to match the thumbnail aspect ratio and edge alignment. Use it as a fit
  reference only; do not include its landscape images in the output.
- Attach
  `assets_src/campaign/ui/campaign_chapter_selector_parchment.png` only as a
  material and color reference for the shared panel behind the frames.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG sprite sheet:
  `campaign_chapter_thumbnail_frames_sheet.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/campaign/chapter-thumbnail-frames/`.
- Canvas: exactly 2000 x 667 pixels, horizontal, RGBA with genuine transparent
  alpha.
- Arrange exactly two equal 1000 x 667 pixel cells side by side:
  1. Current/selected frame on the left.
  2. Other/non-current frame on the right.
- Keep each frame cell at 1000 x 667 pixels with transparent outer margins.
  The visible frame silhouette should be a shallow, wide card that crops to
  about 1.95:1; Android lays it out in a 144 x 74 dp slot and renders the whole
  card at 80% scale (about 115 x 59 dp). The parchment viewport is 312 x 104 dp
  and shows exactly two cards side by side.
- Keep both versions' outer silhouette and transparent window exactly the same
  size and shape. Leave a broad transparent image opening of approximately
  126 x 51 dp (about 2.47:1) for the UI to center-crop a 16:9 thumbnail into;
  this opening renders at about 101 x 41 dp. The thumbnail fills this opening;
  keep the lower edge readable beneath a translucent live chapter-name
  caption.
- Keep the frame trim narrow enough to leave the map preview legible; do not
  fill the transparent window or place generated artwork inside it.

## Frame direction

- Use a shallow rectangular frame with restrained, slightly beveled antique
  gold/bronze trim. Match the campaign screenshot's fantasy UI finish and the
  aged parchment panel without copying its entire card or screen.
- **Current/selected:** brighter warm gold, crisp highlights, and a restrained
  inner edge glow. Make selection immediately readable without overpowering
  the thumbnail.
- **Other/non-current:** the same geometry and materials, with darker,
  subdued bronze/gold and no selection glow. This variant applies equally to
  completed, locked, and preview chapters; progress state is separate from
  selection.
- Keep all ornament attached to the narrow frame. Do not let highlights,
  shadows, or glow extend outside the cell, where they could be clipped or
  overlap neighboring thumbnails.
- Two 144 x 74 dp layout slots fit within the 312 x 104 dp parchment viewport.
  The selector scrolls horizontally to other chapters; preserve the 80% card
  scale and do not show more than two cards at once.

## Separation from thumbnails and live UI

- Generate the two frame overlays only. Do not bake in any map image,
  thumbnail, parchment, card fill, or opaque center.
- Do not add chapter names, numbers, captions, title plaques, letters, runes,
  locks, checkmarks, or other status badges. Android draws text and status
  badges separately.
- Do not create two different frame shapes. Only brightness, gold intensity,
  and selection highlighting may differ between the current and other frame.
- Do not add side panels, ribbons, scroll ends, large corner ornaments,
  medallions, detached decorations, or a full-screen mockup.
- Keep the opening transparent and wide enough to show a recognizable
  panoramic crop of the 16:9 miniature.

## Review and extraction

- Confirm the sheet is exactly 2000 x 667 pixels with two 1000 x 667 RGBA cells
  in Current / Other order.
- Confirm both cells share identical geometry, transparent outer margins, a
  wide image opening, and room for a separate live caption strip.
- Confirm the current frame reads as selected and the other frame remains
  subdued, with no lock/completion imagery baked in.
- Composite both frames over the supplied thumbnail sheet and parchment
  reference. Check that thumbnails and captions remain legible at 80% display
  scale, with exactly two cards fitting within the shared 312 x 104 dp panel.
- After approval, split the actual sheet into:
  `campaign_chapter_thumbnail_frame_current.png` and
  `campaign_chapter_thumbnail_frame_other.png`, each 1000 x 667 RGBA.
- For runtime exports, crop both cells to the same visible frame-content bounds
  while preserving identical dimensions and transparent windows.
- Do not integrate the frames into Android until the generated overlays have
  been reviewed and approved.

## Negative prompt

opaque center, filled card, thumbnail image, landscape, map, parchment
background, square icon, emblem, medallion, large card, separate title plaque,
chapter number, chapter name, text, letters, writing, runes, lock, checkmark,
status badge, different frame geometry, thick border, oversized ornaments,
scroll ends, ribbon, detached glow, detached shadow, particles, neighboring
cells touching, divider, UI screenshot, watermark, signature
